Nice functional geo.

Let  $X$  be an arbitrary point in the plane. Construct four squares around it with side length  $1$  like so:
[asy]
pair A,B,C,D,P,Q,R,S,X;
A=(0,2);
B=(2,2);
C=(2,0);
D=(0,0);
P=(1,2);
Q=(2,1);
R=(1,0);
S=(0,1);
X=(1,1);
dot(A);
dot(B);
dot(C);
dot(D);
dot(P);
dot(Q);
dot(R);
dot(S);
dot(X);
label(A,"A",NW);
label(P,"P",N);
label(B,"B",NE);
label(Q,"Q",E);
label(C,"C",SE);
label(R,"R",N*(-1)); // for some reason S doesn't work here
label(D,"D",SW);
label(S,"S",W);
label(X,"X",SW);
draw(A--B--C--D--A);
draw(P--Q--R--S--Q);
draw(S--P--R);
[/asy]
From this, we get:
\begin{align*}
f(A)+f(P)+f(X)+f(S)&=0,
f(P)+f(B)+f(Q)+f(X)&=0,
f(X)+f(Q)+f(C)+f(R)&=0,
f(S)+f(X)+f(R)+f(D)&=0,
f(A)+f(B)+f(C)+f(D)&=0,
f(P)+f(Q)+f(R)+f(S)&=0.\end{align*}
Adding the first four equations and using the last two yields  $\boxed{f(X)=0}$  for all points  $X$ .

candidates:
[asy]size(120); pathpen = linewidth(1); real r = 0.1, r2 = 2/3*r; path s = (0,0)--(1-r,0)--(1-r,1-r)--(0,1-r)--cycle;
D(shift(r/3,r/3)*s);D(shift(-1+r2,r/3)*s);D(shift(r/3,-1+r2)*s);D(shift(-1+r2,-1+r2)*s); D((-1,-1)--(-1,1)--(1,1)--(1,-1)--cycle,red+linewidth(1));D((0,1)--(1,0)--(0,-1)--(-1,0)--cycle,blue+linewidth(1));
for(int i = -1; i < 2; ++i) for(int j = -1; j < 2; ++j) D((i,j),linewidth(7)); MP("P",(0,0),(2,2));[/asy] Summing  $ f$  over the vertices of the black squares, then subtracting  $ f$  over the vertices of the red square, then subtracting twice of  $ f$  over the vertices of the blue square, gives  $ 4f(P) \equal{} 0$ , and thus  $ f(P)$  is identically zero for all points  $ P$ .

very nice problem!

