We have
    \begin{align*}
        (n+2)A_{n+1}-nA_n &= 2(n+1)^{2k} 
        (n+1)A_n-(n-1)A_{n-1} &= 2n^{2k}
    \end{align*}
    From these we get
    \begin{align*}
        (n+1)(n+2)A_{n+1}-n(n+1)A_n &= 2(n+1)^{2k+1} 
        n(n+1)A_n-(n-1)nA_{n-1} &= 2n^{2k+1} 
        (n+1)(n+2)A_{n+1}-(n-1)nA_{n-1} &= 2(n+1)^{2k+1}+2n^{2k+1}
    \end{align*}
    Using this recurrence, we obtain
    \[A_n=\frac{2S(n)}{n(n+1)},\qquad S(n)=1^{2k+1}+2^{2k+1}+\dots+n^{2k+1}.\]
    Since
    \[2S(n)=\sum_{i=0}^n \left((n-i)^{2k+1}+i^{2k+1}\right)=\sum_{i=1}^n \left((n+1-i)^{2k+1}+i^{2k+1}\right)\]
    we see that  $n(n+1)|2S(n)$ . Thus  $A_n$  is an integer for all  $n$ . Next we show that  $A_n$  is odd iff  $n\equiv 1$  or  $2\pmod{4}$ .

    If  $n\equiv 1$  or  $2\pmod{4}$ , then  $S(n)$  is odd since it has an odd number of odd terms. Thus  $A_n$  is odd.

    If  $n\equiv 0\pmod{4}$ , then  $(n/2)^{2k+1}\equiv 0\pmod{n}$ . Thus
    \[S(n)=\sum_{i=0}^{n/2}\left((n-i)^{2k+1}+i^{2k+1}\right)-\left(\frac{n}{2}\right)^t\equiv 0\pmod{n}\qquad\Rightarrow\qquad A_n\text{ is even.}\]

    If  $n\equiv 3\pmod{4}$ , then  $\left((n+1)/2\right)^{2k+1}\equiv 0\pmod{n+1}$ . Thus
    \[S(n)=\sum_{i=1}^{(n+1)/2} \left((n+1-i)^{2k+1}+i^{2k+1}\right)-\left(\frac{n+1}{2}\right)^{2k+1}\equiv 0\pmod{n+1} \qquad\Rightarrow\qquad A_n\text{ is even.}\]

