WLOG, suppose  $a_1 \leq a_2 \leq \cdots \leq a_n$ . By Cauchy, we have
	\begin{align*}
		\left(n + \frac {1}{2}\right)^2 &\geq \left((a_1 + a_n) + \sum_{i = 2}^{n - 1} a_i\right)\left(\left(\frac{1}{a_1} + \frac{1}{a_n}\right) + \sum_{i = 2}^{n - 1} \frac{1}{a_i}\right) 
		&\geq \left(\sqrt{(a_1 + a_n)\left(\frac{1}{a_1} + \frac{1}{a_n}\right)} + (n - 2)\right)^2.
	\end{align*}	
Let  $t = \frac{a_n}{a_1}$ . Then, we have
	\begin{align*}
		\left(n + \frac{1}{2}\right)^2 &\geq \left(\sqrt{2 + t + \frac{1}{t}} + (n - 2)\right)^2 
		\iff \left(n + \frac{1}{2}\right) &\geq \left(\sqrt{2 + t + \frac{1}{t}} + (n - 2)\right) 
		\iff \frac{5}{2} &\geq \sqrt{2 + t + \frac{1}{t}} 
		\iff 4t^2 - 17t + 4 &\leq 0 
		\iff (4t - 1)(t - 4) &\leq 0.
	\end{align*}
Therefore, we have
	\begin{align*}
		\frac{1}{4} \leq t \leq 4.
	\end{align*}
Thus, 
	\begin{align*}
		a_n \leq 4a_1,
	\end{align*}
as desired.  $\Box$

We have that
