Define points as in the figure. WLOG  $AB = 2$ . First we show  $\frac{AX}{XH}  = \frac{2}{5}$ . Using Menelaus Theorem in  $\triangle AXB$  wrt line  $\overline{XU}$  and in  $\triangle ABV$  wrt line  $\overline{FU}$  gives (we will use  $FA = AV = 2$  since  $\triangle ABV$  is equilateral):  $$  \frac{AX}{XH} = \frac{BU}{HU} ~~ \text{and} ~~ \frac{BU}{UV} = \frac{AF}{FV} = \frac{1}{2} \implies UV = \frac{4}{3}, BU = \frac{2}{3} \qquad \therefore ~ \frac{AX}{XH} = \frac{\frac{2}{3}}{\frac{5}{3}} = \frac{2}{5}  $$  Now by Cosine rule in  $\triangle ABH$ ,   $$  AH = \sqrt{2^2 + 1^2 +2 \cdot 1} = \sqrt{7} \implies AX = \frac{2}{\sqrt{7}} $$  So using  $HA \cdot HT = HB \cdot HC$  we obtain 
