\begin{align*}
OP^2 = 2^2 - \left( \frac{4}{\sqrt{7}} \right)^2 = 4 - \frac{16}{7} = \frac{12}{7}  \implies OX = \sqrt{ \left( \frac{2}{\sqrt{7}} \right)^2 +  OP^2} = \sqrt{ \frac{4}{7} + \frac{12}{7} } = \frac{4}{\sqrt{7}}
\end{align*}
Finally, we have   $$  \frac{\text{area of blue hexagon}}{\text{area of red hexagon}} = \left( \frac{OX}{OA} \right)^2 =  \left( \frac{2}{\sqrt{7}} \right)^2 = \boxed{\frac{4}{7}}  $$

