\begin{align*}
F &= \frac{ BC(A + F') - AF'(B+C)}{BC - AF'} 
&= \frac{y^2z^2(x^2 + \frac{y^2z^2}{t^2}) - \frac{x^2y^2z^2}{t^2} (y^2 + z^2)}{y^2z^2 - \frac{x^2y^2z^2}{t^2}} 
&= \frac{x^2 t^2 + y^2z^2 - x^2y^2 - x^2z^2}{t^2 - x^2} .
\end{align*}
Thus 
\[ G = \frac{F+ I}{2} = \frac{x^2 t^2 + y^2z^2 - x^2y^2 - x^2z^2 - (t^2-x^2)(xy + yz + zx)}{2(t^2-x^2)}. \]
------
Next, we solve for  $K$ . Since  $K$  lies on  $EI$ , we have that 
\begin{align*}
K &= \frac{E - I}{E\overline{I} -1} 
&= \frac{t^2 + xy + yz + zx}{-t^2( \frac{1}{xy} + \frac{1}{yz} + \frac{1}{zx}) - 1} 
&= \frac{-xyz(t^2 + xy + yz + zx)}{t^2 (x + y + z) + xyz}
\end{align*}
------
Now let  $\alpha = \frac{G-D}{K-D}$ . We want to check that  $\alpha \in \mathbb{R}$ . Equivalently,  $\alpha = \overline{\alpha}$ . First, we conduct some simplifications to  $\alpha$ . 
