The answer is yes. In what follows, we represent positions of the board using ordered tuples.**Lemma:** We can go from  $(n, 0, 0)$  to  $(0, 2^n, 0)$ .

*Proof:* We have 
\begin{align*}
	(n, 0, 0) \to (n - 1, 2, 0) \to (n - 1, 0, 4) \to (n - 2, 4, 0) \to (n - 2, 0, 8) \to 
(n - 3, 8, 0) \to \cdots \to (n - n, 2^n, 0) \equiv (0, 2^n, 0). \hspace{0.2in} \blacksquare
\end{align*}

Furthermore, we claim that  $2^{2^{2^{18} - 1}} > 2010^{2010^{2010}}$ . Indeed, 
\begin{align*}
