Proving  $AP=AQ$  is the same as proving  $APQ$  is isosceles, or  $\angle APQ = \angle AQP.$  Note  $\angle ACB = \angle APQ$  since  $ACBP$  is cyclic. Furthermore, since  $\angle AFC = \angle ADC$  we know  $AFDC$  is cyclic. Similarly  $BFEC$  is cyclic. Notice  $\angle AFQ = 180^\circ - \angle AFD = \angle ACB.$  Thus, since  $\angle APQ = \angle AFQ$  we know  $AFPQ$  is cyclic. Finally, \[\angle AQP = 180^\circ- \angle PFB = 180^\circ - \angle EFB = \angle ACB.\] Therefore,  $\angle APQ = \angle AQP = \angle ACB,$  as required.

